# agent-chrome.sh profiles: one name=port line each (CDP on 127.0.0.1), optionally ` app=<Application name>`.
# Copy to ~/.config/jadlis/agent-chrome.conf. Without this file agent-chrome.sh knows one profile: agent=9333.
# Another profile: add a line here AND a matching pw-<name> server (same port) in ~/.claude/agents/browser-operator.md.
# No `app=` → the profile runs in Google Chrome. `app=Google Chrome Beta` keeps the agent apart from your own Chrome;
# moving an existing profile to another app needs its cookies carried over (references/gotchas.md).
# The default profile is BROWSER_PROFILE in ~/.config/jadlis/agent.conf (or `agent`).
agent=9333
# work=9334 app=Google Chrome Beta
